# s2a-del-ipc-handlers: desktop wire (for DELETE-HOT-G11)

The seven ipc-*.ts modules no longer register a handler for a DIRECT key (shared/desktop-api-split.ts DIRECT_KEYS). The signatures
below changed, so the hot files must change in the same batch (apps/desktop tsc fails on ipc.ts until they do):

## apps/desktop/src/main/ipc.ts (registerDesktopIpc)

- Delete `import { registerNotificationIpc } from './ipc-notifications';` and its call `registerNotificationIpc({ handle, invokeDesktopOperation, core: protocol });`
  (ipc-notifications.ts is deleted: all five channels are DIRECT keys, answered by renderer/core-direct/api-settings.ts).
- `registerFileDialogIpc({ ... })`: remove the property `app: serviceApp`.
- `registerProjectIpc({ handle, host, shell, invokeDesktopOperation, operations: serviceOperations, core: localCore })` becomes
  `registerProjectIpc({ handle, host, shell, core: localCore })`.
- `registerProjectFileIpc({ ... })`: remove the property `app: serviceApp`.
- `registerSessionIpc({ ... })` becomes `registerSessionIpc({ handle, remoteHosts, core: protocol })` (no host, invokeDesktopOperation, browserHost,
  remoteAccessInfo, rotateRemoteAccess, revokeRemoteAccessClient).
- `registerWindowSettingsIpc({ ... })` becomes
  `registerWindowSettingsIpc({ window, app, handle, invokeDesktopOperation, settingsStore, previewNotificationSound })`
  (no host, readsLocalOnboardingStatus, raiseOnSignIn, pcHost, onDesktopSettingsChanged, confirmAllowAllActions,
  writesAnnounceThemselves, pcCore). `confirmAllowAllActions` stays for registerHostExtrasIpc.
- `registerSourceControlIpc({ ... })`: remove the property `operations: serviceOperations`.
- Then dead in ipc.ts, delete: the SERVICE_OPERATION_NAMES table, `type ServiceOperation`, `serviceOperation`, `serviceOperations`, `serviceGetPath`,
  `serviceApp` (and the `serviceUserDataPath` dependency, the option and its destructuring), the dependency fields and destructured names
  `onDesktopSettingsChanged`, `remoteAccessInfo`, `rotateRemoteAccess`, `revokeRemoteAccessClient`, and the imports `DesktopRemoteAccessInfo`,
  `DesktopSettings` (if tsc reports them unused). `browserHost` stays (registerBrowserIpc); drop 'releaseSession' from its Pick only if tsc agrees.
  `settingsStore`'s Pick may shrink to 'readZoom' | 'updateZoom'.
- The DIRECT handlers' channels are no longer registered, so `channels` (the dispose list) needs no change: it removes whatever DESKTOP_IPC names.

## apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts

- In the registerDesktopIpc options: remove `onDesktopSettingsChanged: applyDesktopSettings` (the core's settings change reaches `applyDesktopSettings` through
  core-observers.ts), `remoteAccessInfo`, `rotateRemoteAccess`, `revokeRemoteAccessClient` and `serviceUserDataPath`, and the three functions of index.ts
  (`remoteAccessInfo`, `rotateRemoteAccess`, `revokeRemoteAccessClient`) when nothing else calls them (line 1355 does: keep that one).

## apps/desktop/src/main/ipc-state-bridge.ts (amendment of the open-findings audit; the last s2a deletion task applies it)

Reduce it to the pushes a live renderer subscribes to: remove the old-lane pushes no renderer listens to (sessionsChanged, agentPoolChanged, folderChanged,
the lsp* pushes and the rest) once `subscribeSessions`, `subscribeAgentPool`, `subscribeFolderChanges`, `subscribeLspDiagnostics`, `subscribeLspStatus`
(all DIRECT keys of renderer/core-direct) are the only listeners.

## Other files (not owned by this task)

- apps/desktop/src/main/desktop-service-contract.ts: drop the optional members `readSessionTranscript?` and `readSessionHistory?` and the two names in
  DESKTOP_SERVICE_METHODS (this task removed both from desktop-service-client.ts and shared/core-lanes/session-lane.ts).
- Tests that still import a removed handler (the s2a-del-ipc-tests task): ipc-notifications.test.mjs (delete), ipc-projects.test.mjs, ipc-core-callers.test.mjs,
  ipc-sessions-device-alias.test.mjs, ipc-sessions-favorite.test.mjs, approval-grant-change.test.mjs, core-session-route.test.mjs, session-history-boundary.test.mjs
  (its list of files naming readSessionHistory is now empty), protocol/session-lane.test.mjs (the "whole conversation" case), ipc-window-pc-quota.test.mjs,
  developer-risk-confirm.test.mjs, settings-store.test.mjs, connections/model-login.test.mjs, local-page-permissions.test.mjs, ipc-file-dialogs.test.mjs
  (the download cases stay).
- Rust: the operation names `readSessionTranscript` and `readSessionHistory` in mixdog-app-protocol schema/operations_map.json, inventory.rs and
  mixdog-core-domains desktop_residual.rs have no caller left; the protocol lead removes them with the next [remove] section.
